course: dictionary
lesson: 6347
title: Words that travelled from French
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: After 1066, French-speaking lords ruled England, and English and French mixed. Farmers kept English names for their animals, but the meat eaten at the lord's table got French names. «Mouton» is the French word for sheep, and it is also the source of the English word mutton, which means sheep meat.
explain: Mouton has a second meaning in English. It is sheepskin that has been treated to look like beaver or seal fur, and it is used for coats. The word is uncountable, so you say some mouton, not a mouton.
explain: Use context to find the meaning. In the song «Il pleut, il pleut, bergère», the words «blancs moutons» mean white sheep. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Mouton» is the French word for sheep.
fact: In English, «mutton» means sheep meat, and it comes from French «mouton».
fact: Beef comes from «bœuf», pork from «porc», and mutton from «mouton», while the animals kept English names.
fact: In English, «mouton» can mean sheepskin treated to look like beaver or seal fur, used for coats.
fact: In English lessons, say «sheep» for the animal, not «mouton».
exercise: Where does the English word mutton come from? | Australian word «servo» | English word «sheep» | *French word «mouton» | Scots word «dreich»
exercise: On the farm in 1100, the English farmer looks after a sheep. What does the French lord call that animal's meat? | *Mutton | Pork | Veal | Beef
exercise: In «Il pleut, il pleut, bergère», what does «blancs moutons» mean? | Red meat | Fat shepherds | Little white clouds | *White sheep
test: In English, what is «mouton» when it is used for coats? | Real beaver fur | *Sheepskin treated to look like beaver or seal fur | Leather from cows | Shaved sheep wool
test: Why do we not use «mouton» as an ordinary English word for the animal? | *Because in English we say sheep | It means cow in English | It is a Scots word | It is only a word for a coat
exam: Which statement about «mouton» is correct? | *It is French for sheep, and English took it for mutton | It means beef in English | It is an ordinary English word for a sheep | It is a Scots word for a coat
